Key Type Default Meaning <code>z_method</code> text <code>"Absolute z position"</code> or <code>"Height above Membrane"</code> <code>distance_to_mem</code> nm <code>2.0</code> gap between membrane surface and lowest protein bead (Height above Membrane) <code>randomize_pos</code> true/false <code>false</code> random x/y position <code>randomize_pos_every</code> true/false <code>false</code> a new random position for every system <code>randomize_rot</code> true/false <code>false</code> random orientation <code>randomize_rot_every</code> true/false <code>false</code> a new random orientation for every system <code>use_protein_distance</code> true/false <code>false</code> two proteins: place them by their gap <code>protein_distance</code> nm <code>1.0</code> that gap <code>more_copies</code> true/false <code>false</code> several copies of one protein <code>copy_number</code> number <code>2</code> copies per system <code>copy_mode</code> text <code>"together"</code> <code>"together"</code> (grid, shared orientation) or <code>"independent"</code> (own pose per copy) <code>copy_params</code> list <code>[]</code> independent copies: <code>[{"cx", "cy", "cz", "rx", "ry", "rz"}, …]</code> <code>randomize_rot_all_copies</code> true/false <code>false</code> copies "together": a random orientation for each copy <code>protein_params</code> object the pose of every protein in every system, see below <code>insertion_params</code> object the settings of the protein insertion page, per protein (used to restore the page) <p><code>protein_params</code> holds the position (nm from the box centre) and rotation (degrees) used for each protein in each system:</p> <pre><code>"protein_params": {
    "R0001": {"1UBQ.pdb": {"cx": 0.0, "cy": 0.0, "cz": 4.12, "rx": 0.0, "ry": 0.0, "rz": 0.0}},
    "R0002": {"1UBQ.pdb": {"cx": 0.0, "cy": 0.0, "cz": 4.12, "rx": 0.0, "ry": 0.0, "rz": 0.0}}
}
</code></pre> <p>Independent copies add a <code>"copies": [ … ]</code> list with the pose of every copy. Fixed (not random) positions and rotations are taken from <code>R0001</code> for all systems.</p>
